---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
const title='PDR Service Area | Greeley & Northern Colorado';
const description='Peak Country provides mobile auto hail repair and paintless dent repair by appointment in Greeley, Weld County, and nearby Northern Colorado communities.';
const pageSchema={ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'Service','@id':`${site.url}/service-area/#service`,name:'Mobile Paintless Dent Repair Service',description,url:`${site.url}/service-area/`,provider:{'@id':`${site.url}/#business`},areaServed:[{ '@type':'City',name:'Greeley, Colorado'},{'@type':'AdministrativeArea',name:'Weld County, Colorado'},...site.approvedCommunities.filter(name=>name!=='Greeley').map(name=>({'@type':'City',name:`${name}, Colorado`})),{'@type':'Place',name:'Northern Colorado'}] };
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} exactTitle pageSchema={pageSchema}>
  <header class="page-head area-head"><div class="eyebrow">Mobile service · By appointment</div><h1>Paintless Dent Repair Service Area in Greeley and Northern Colorado</h1><p>Peak Country is a service-area business providing mobile auto hail repair, door ding repair, and PDR around Greeley, Weld County, and nearby Northern Colorado communities.</p><div class="about-actions"><a class="button" href="/free-hail-inspection/">Request a Free Inspection →</a><a class="text-link" href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>Call {site.phoneDisplay} →</a></div></header>
  <section class="section area-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">Primary Service Area</div><h2>Greeley, Colorado</h2><p>Greeley is the primary geographic anchor for Peak Country’s mobile service. Vehicle owners can request an inspection for hail damage, parking-lot door dings, minor dents, and repairable creases without the website representing a walk-in storefront or a separate city office.</p><p>Mobile availability depends on the vehicle’s location, safe working space, weather, lighting needs, access to power when applicable, and the scope of the repair. Appointment details and the service location are confirmed directly before work is scheduled.</p></div><aside><strong>Service-area business</strong><p>Mobile by appointment. No public walk-in address is advertised.</p></aside></section>
  <section class="area-band"><div class="section"><div><div class="eyebrow">Weld County Communities</div><h2>Local coverage around Greeley</h2><p>Peak Country serves customers in Greeley and considers mobile appointments throughout Weld County, including Evans, Windsor, Eaton, Severance, Johnstown, Milliken, LaSalle, and Platteville. These communities describe the practical working area; they are not separate shops, offices, or staffed locations.</p><p>Service may also extend to surrounding Northern Colorado communities. Distance, scheduling, repair scope, and a suitable work environment are reviewed individually. If you are outside the listed cities, include your city or ZIP when requesting an inspection so availability can be confirmed accurately.</p></div><ul aria-label="Communities served">{site.approvedCommunities.map(name=><li>{name}</li>)}</ul></div></section>
  <article class="section area-content">
    <section><h2>Mobile auto hail repair</h2><p>Northern Colorado hail can affect multiple panels across one vehicle. Peak Country’s <a href="/auto-hail-repair/">auto hail repair service</a> begins with a direct inspection under appropriate reflection lighting. Dent depth, paint condition, metal stretch, body-line location, panel material, and access help determine which damage may qualify for PDR.</p><p>The mobile setting must support safe inspection and repair. Some extensive repairs, access requirements, weather conditions, or vehicle circumstances may affect what can reasonably be completed at a particular location. Those details are discussed before scheduling rather than assumed from a photograph.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Paintless dent repair and everyday dents</h2><p><a href="/paintless-dent-repair/">Paintless dent repair</a> may preserve original factory paint on suitable hail dents, door dings, minor dents, and creases. It is not the right method for every panel. Cracked paint, excessive metal stretch, previous bodywork, structural conditions, or limited access may lead to another repair recommendation.</p><p>Peak Country’s mobile model keeps the work technician-led. The person assessing repairability is focused on the actual panel and the conditions needed to handle the vehicle carefully. Review the <a href="/repair-standards/">Peak Country PDR repair standards</a> for more detail about access, protection, reassembly, and final quality checks.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Regional hail information</h2><p>The <a href="/hail-tracker/">Northern Colorado Hail Tracker</a> provides official-source context from National Weather Service alerts and preliminary Storm Prediction Center reports. Dedicated views are available for <a href="/hail-tracker/greeley/">reported hail around Greeley</a>, <a href="/hail-tracker/weld-county/">Weld County hail reports</a>, and the broader <a href="/hail-tracker/northern-colorado/">Northern Colorado hail-report area</a>.</p><p>Weather reports do not prove that a specific vehicle was struck or damaged. Coverage and location precision vary, and observations can be delayed or corrected. The <a href="/northern-colorado-hail-history/">verified historical hail archive</a> uses completed 2016–2025 NOAA/NCEI data separately from current preliminary reports. A vehicle inspection remains the basis for identifying damage and discussing repairability.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Requesting service</h2><p>Include the vehicle year, make and model, the type of damage, and the city or ZIP where the vehicle is located. Photos can help begin the conversation, but they may not show shallow dents, paint condition, metal stretch, or access behind the panel. A request is not a confirmed appointment until Peak Country responds with availability and location details.</p><p>To get started, <a href="/free-hail-inspection/">request a free hail or dent inspection</a>, use the <a href="/contact/">Peak Country contact options</a>, or call or text <a href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>. Service-area questions are welcome, especially for locations outside the listed Weld County communities.</p></section>
  </article>
</Layout>
